 "result": "I read all 20 modules in order, start to finish, without grep.\n\n## Functions that divide without checking for zero\n\nFive functions do `return total / parts` with no check, so `parts == 0` raises `ZeroDivisionError`:\n\n| Module | Function | Line |\n|---|---|---|\n| calc/n02.py | `share_n02(total, parts)` | `calc/n02.py:5` |\n| calc/n07.py | `share_n07(total, parts)` | `calc/n07.py:5` |\n| calc/n11.py | `share_n11(total, parts)` | `calc/n11.py:5` |\n| calc/n15.py | `share_n15(total, parts)` | `calc/n15.py:5` |\n| calc/n19.py | `share_n19(total, parts)` | `calc/n19.py:5` |\n\nThe other 15 `share_nXX` functions check `if parts == 0: return 0` before dividing. None of the other functions divide at all. The many `step_*` functions only multiply, add, compare and take `sqrt(abs(...))`. `retry_policy`, `archive` and `close_books` don't divide either.\n\n## Answers\n\n- **(a)** `MAX_BATCH = 384` (`calc/n04.py:9`).\n- **(b)** `retry_policy()` is defined in **calc/n13.py** (`calc/n13.py:9`). It returns `min(attempt * 2, 20)`.\n- **(c)** In calc/n17.py, **`close_books(rows)`** calls `archive()` (`calc/n17.py:13-14`).\n\nOne small thing: each file's docstring names a different module than its filename. For example, n01.py says `\"calc.m21\"` and n20.py says `\"calc.m40\"`. This doesn't change any answer above, but it could confuse anyone who goes by the docstrings.",
